Description: Look for post_boot script in /usr/libexec in addition to /etc
 The post_boot init scripts shipped by userspace-resource-manager-extensions
 are currently installed into /etc/urm/initscripts/post_boot/. That location
 is wrong: these are vendor-provided executables, not configuration, so per
 Debian Policy 9.1.1 they belong under /usr. Installing them below /etc also
 makes them conffiles, causing dpkg to prompt on upgrade for files that
 administrators are not expected to edit directly.
 .
 Add an additional ExecStartPre pointing at the /usr/libexec location, so that
 the unit keeps working once the extensions package installs its scripts to
 the correct path. Both lines are prefixed with "-", so a missing script at
 either location is ignored and only the layout actually present takes effect.
Author: Lukas Märdian <lukas.maerdian@oss.qualcomm.com>
Bug: https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/pkg-urm-ext/issues/23
Forwarded: https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/pkg-urm-ext/issues/23
Last-Update: 2026-08-10

--- a/urm.service.in
+++ b/urm.service.in
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 [Service]
 Restart=on-failure
 ExecStart=@CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_BINDIR@/urm
+ExecStartPre=-/usr/libexec/urm/initscripts/post_boot/post_boot.sh
 ExecStartPre=-/etc/urm/initscripts/post_boot/post_boot.sh
 TimeoutStopSec=2
 Delegate=yes
